   "html_text": "Michelle Dempsey (2009) argues that when victims do not support prosecutions of domestic violence, prosecutors should respond as feminists. By this, she means that prosecutors should act on reasons guided by a commitment to reconstitute their communities to lessen the influence of patriarchy in the form of structural inequality that systematically limits women’s lives. In developing her argument, Dempsey draws on her own experience as a prosecutor who had pursued strong pro-prosecution policies ",
   "md_text": "Michelle Dempsey (2009) argues that when victims do not support prosecutions of domestic violence, prosecutors should respond as feminists. By this, she means that prosecutors should act on reasons guided by a commitment to reconstitute their communities to lessen the influence of patriarchy in the form of structural inequality that systematically limits women’s lives. In developing her argument, Dempsey draws on her own experience as a prosecutor who had pursued strong pro-prosecution policies "
